-- E-commerce & CRM module entities. Note: `EcomProfile` is prefixed
-- because the system-tier `profile` (fenel/std/entities/profile.fenel,
-- Phase 3d) is a rich 10-field identity model (type / gender /
-- firstName / lastName / email / phone / dob / avatar / notes /
-- nicknames). This module's lightweight 5-field CRM contact shape
-- lives alongside as a distinct entity. type-catalog.ts:1056 silently
-- keeps the first registration on collision, and system entities
-- register before module entities — pre-rename, ecom's `profile` was
-- shadowed and unreachable. Same module-prefix convention as notion's
-- `NotionUser` / `NotionColor` for cross-module collision avoidance.
--
-- `Asset` PascalCase-normalizes ecom's old lowercase `asset` codename
-- to align with Phase 3d's system-tier convention. No live consumers
-- reference the lowercase codename (grep audit confirmed); free
-- normalization.
--
-- Field refs: `email: EmailStr` / `phone: PhoneStr` reuse refined-
-- String atoms declared in profile.fenel; `url: UrlStr` reuses the
-- one declared in proxy_link.fenel. They resolve through the catalog
-- at load time (both land in foundationTemplates().entities before
-- any module's load fires).
--
-- `customData: {}` is the known empty-record placeholder (AGENTS.md
-- flags this as an anti-pattern for dynamic-shape data; future
-- cleanup target — should model via dependent `$el` or
-- `Map<String, Json>`). Mirrors AIResponse's `Parsed value: {}` from
-- Phase 4b.

EcomProfile = EcomProfile email: EmailStr phone: PhoneStr name: String tags: List String customData: {}

Asset = Asset hash: String url: UrlStr name: String size: Number mimeType: String width: Maybe<Number> height: Maybe<Number> duration: Maybe<Number> pages: Maybe<Number>
